   "by": "owner",
   "basis": "owner-ruled 2026-10-25 (A63)",
   "question": "The statute review packet for citation-bench#30: 46 one-line answers on existence, written forms, code abbreviations and span patterns, plus the two contradicted vectors",
   "answer": "Accept the packet's answer sheet. Conn. Practice Book is one code; N.Y. Family Ct Act keeps New York's own style; Pa. Stat. Ann. for P.S.; \"(Rev. to year)\" and \"(1969 Reenactment)\" stay inside the span and are not recorded as year; conn_gen_stat/1's \"10 -236b\" is not decided and stays unverified; the two Attorney General opinion vectors (ark_aca/1, la_rev_stat/0) stay, and the README says the set includes citations as courts and state attorneys general write them. vt_vsa/0 is accepted as is; nm_nmsa/0 is fixed by re-taking its excerpt from the same opinion."
  }
 },
